! ---- System aperture types: NAO (CODE V object NA), FLOAT (pupil floats
! with the stop's clear aperture), and the per-plane SAY/SAX they build on.
!
! NAO needs a finite object distance: LithoKotaro (4x reduction).  NAO 0.1
! gives image NA 0.4, i.e. F/1.25 working.
CV2PRG LithoKotaro.seq
NAO
NAO 0.1
NAO
FIR
! Saved as EPD in the lens block plus NAO after GO; CODE V (NAO) and Zemax
! (OBNA) round trips.  (Both importers used to send 'NAO,', which the engine
! does not have, so the object NA was dropped.)
SAV natest
RES osdtriplet
RES natest
NAO
ZOA2CV natest.seq
RES osdtriplet
CV2PRG natest.seq
NAO
ZOA2ZMX natest.zmx
RES osdtriplet
ZMX2PRG natest.zmx
NAO
FIR
! Errors: object at infinity, out of range
RES osdtriplet
NAO 0.1
NAO 1.5
!
! FLOAT: with a 2 mm stop the pupil is 10 * 2 / 3.912 = 5.112 (the marginal
! ray meets the stop at 3.912 when EPD is 10); it follows the stop size.
! (SAY FLOAT never took effect: a SYSTEM()->setter migration dropped the
! IF(WQ.EQ.'FLOAT') guards, so the flag was set and cleared at once.)
CIR S3 2
FLOAT
FIR
CIR S3 3
FIR
! .zoa restores FLOAT; Zemax carries it as FLOA plus the stop's CLAP; CODE V
! has no float, so the .seq holds the current EPD.
SAV fltest
RES osdtriplet
RES fltest
FIR
ZOA2ZMX fltest.zmx
RES osdtriplet
ZMX2PRG fltest.zmx
FIR
RES fltest
ZOA2CV fltest.seq
RES osdtriplet
CV2PRG fltest.seq
FIR
! EPD replaces FLOAT
EPD 10
FIR
FLOAT 2
!
! SAY and SAX are independent (the same migration made each set both);
! EPD sets both (one circular pupil).
RES osdtriplet
EPD 12
SAY
SAX
U L
SAX, 3
EOS
SAY
SAX
EPD 14
SAY
SAX
